From 395cc3fdab77f8fae3a8ae1b14db2b79ae5e145c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerasim Troeglazov <3dEyes@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 10:53:19 +1000
Subject: Add Haiku platform support with dual-backend build

Based on patches sourced from https://github.com/kenz-gelsoft/gecko-dev/

- Build System & Architecture:
  * Added Haiku target with dual-backend support: native UI and GTK3 + Wayland.
  * Adjusted compiler and linker flags

- Native UI & System Integration (widget/haiku):
  * Implemented native windowing and view backend (BWindow/BView) with
    software double-buffered rendering via Skia.
  * Implemented native file dialogs (BFilePanel), clipboard (BClipboard),
    custom/system cursors (BCursor), and input method support (IME).
  * Implemented advanced Drag & Drop with support for files, text, images,
    and bookmarks.
  * Implemented desktop notifications via BNotification.
  * Implemented single-instance remote IPC using Haiku kernel ports.
  * Implemented shell services (MIME associations, Tracker wallpaper).
  * Added `moz-icon:` channel for native vector (HVIF) and MIME icons.

- Graphics & Multimedia:
  * Implemented native WebGL context provider via Haiku BGLView.
  * Implemented native cubeb audio backend for MediaKit.
  * Implemented WebRTC desktop screen capture and webcam video capture.
  * Implemented Gamepad API backend using BJoystick.

- Platform Compatibility & Third-Party:
  * Adjusted networking and socket options across libwebrtc, nICEr,
    nrappkit, SCTP, and quinn-udp for Haiku network stack.
  * Fixed type collisions (int64) and compatibility issues in vendored
    Rust crates (glslopt, iana-time-zone-haiku, lmdb-rkv-sys).

